IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `er6-part-vi-alternate-access`

-- Tests of reg 93 (Part VI). Expected values are written from the text of reg 93 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1709-1722), not from the rules.
-- Argument order of reg 93(1): employed in insurable employment now; has been employed in insurable employment; qualifies under
-- section 7 of the Act; the reason for the benefits; has had an interruption of earnings; hours in the qualifying period.

§ `reg 93(1) who qualifies`

-- "(b) has had 600 or more hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period": 599 is not enough, 600 and 601 are.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 599)
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 601
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 0)
-- "(a) has had an interruption of earnings from employment; and (b) ...": both are needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` FALSE 1200)
-- "An insured person who does not qualify to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act": a person who does qualify under section 7 is not this regulation's.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE TRUE `pregnancy` TRUE 1200)
-- "who is claiming special benefits": regular benefits are not special benefits (s 2(1)); each of the six special reasons is.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE 1200)
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `care or support of a family member` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `care or support of a critically ill child` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE `care or support of a critically ill adult` TRUE 600
-- "An insured person": a person is an insured person if they are or have been employed in insurable employment (s 2(1)).
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 600
#ASSERT `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 600
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE 600)

§ `reg 93(2) the benefit period, and the weeks payable`

#ASSERT `reg 93(2) a benefit period is established for the insured person notwithstanding section 9 of the Act` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(2) a benefit period is established for the insured person notwithstanding section 9 of the Act` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(2) a benefit period is established for the insured person notwithstanding section 9 of the Act` FALSE TRUE)

-- A benefit period of 52 whole weeks, Sunday 4 January 2026 to Saturday 2 January 2027.
`test benefit period` MEANS `Period of days` WITH
    `first day of the period` IS YMD 2026 1 4
    `last day of the period` IS YMD 2027 1 2

`test week in` first MEANS `Period of days` WITH
    `first day of the period` IS first
    `last day of the period` IS first PLUS 6

#ASSERT `reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` TRUE TRUE (`test week in` (YMD 2026 1 4)) `test benefit period`
#ASSERT `reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` TRUE TRUE (`test week in` (YMD 2026 12 27)) `test benefit period`
-- the week before the benefit period begins, and the week after it ends, do not fall in it
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` TRUE TRUE (`test week in` (YMD 2025 12 28)) `test benefit period`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` TRUE TRUE (`test week in` (YMD 2027 1 3)) `test benefit period`)
-- "for each week of unemployment": a week that is not one is not paid
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` TRUE FALSE (`test week in` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `test benefit period`)
-- no benefit period established, no payment
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` FALSE TRUE (`test week in` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `test benefit period`)

§ `reg 93(3) sections 22 to 23.3 of the Act apply`

#ASSERT `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 22
#ASSERT `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 23
#ASSERT `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 23.1
#ASSERT `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 23.2
#ASSERT `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 23.3
-- section 21 (illness for a minor attachment claimant) and section 24 are outside "sections 22 to 23.3"
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 21)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` TRUE 24)
-- "special benefits under this section": only for a person who qualifies under subsection (1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` FALSE 22)

§ `reg 93(4.1) the day it comes into force, and what it relieves`

-- the day the subsection comes into force is not in the text; the tests use 2020-01-05 as an invented day, only to test the comparison
#ASSERT `reg 93(4.1) the week begins on or after the day on which the subsection comes into force` (YMD 2020 1 5) (YMD 2020 1 5)
#ASSERT `reg 93(4.1) the week begins on or after the day on which the subsection comes into force` (YMD 2020 1 12) (YMD 2020 1 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4.1) the week begins on or after the day on which the subsection comes into force` (YMD 2020 1 4) (YMD 2020 1 5))
-- all three conditions: a benefit under any of ss 23 to 23.3, a claim because of illness, injury or quarantine, a week on or after the day
#ASSERT `reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `reg 93(4) payment for a working day`

-- argument order: proves unable to work because of illness etc. (40(4) or (5)); proves would otherwise be available; (4.1) relieves the claimant of proving it; proves entitled under ss 22 to 23.3
-- (a) proved in full
#ASSERT `reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (a) proved but not availability, and subsection (4.1) does not relieve: refused
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (a) proved but not availability, and subsection (4.1) relieves: not refused
#ASSERT `reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- availability alone is not enough, even with (4.1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b) proved: not refused
#ASSERT `reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- nothing proved: refused
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits`

-- argument order: received special benefits under this regulation; hours accumulated since the benefit period began; hours in the
-- qualifying period; the hours in the s 7(2) table for the rate at the start of the benefit period; benefits payable under the Act
-- on the qualifying-period hours; section 18 does not bar payment.
-- 100 + 600 = 700, which equals the table's 700: "equal or exceed"
#ASSERT `reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` TRUE 100 600 700 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` TRUE 101 600 700 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` TRUE 99 600 700 TRUE TRUE)
-- (a) the claimant must have received special benefits under this regulation
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` FALSE 100 600 700 TRUE TRUE)
-- (b) benefits must be payable in the benefit period under the Act on the qualifying-period hours
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` TRUE 100 600 700 FALSE TRUE)
-- "Subject to section 18 of the Act"
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` TRUE 100 600 700 TRUE FALSE)

§ `reg 93(6) the rest of the Act and the Regulations apply`

#ASSERT `reg 93(6) a provision of the Act or of the Regulations applies to the claimant` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(6) a provision of the Act or of the Regulations applies to the claimant` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 93(6) a provision of the Act or of the Regulations applies to the claimant` FALSE FALSE)
